      "raw_utf8": "\\begin{thebibliography}{1}\n\n\\bibitem{berdine2006}\nJosh Berdine, Byron Cook, Dino Distefano, and Peter O'Hearn.\n\\newblock Automatic termination proofs for programs with shape-shifting heaps.\n\\newblock In {\\em Computer Aided Verification (CAV)}, 2006.\n\\newblock Primary author prepublication version; Example 8.\n\n\\bibitem{holroyd2008}\nAlexander~E. Holroyd, Lionel Levine, Karola M{\\'e}sz{\\'a}ros, Yuval Peres,\n  James Propp, and David~B. Wilson.\n\\newblock Chip-firing and rotor-routing on directed graphs.\n\\newblock arXiv:0801.3306, 2008.\n\\newblock Primary preprint; Theorem 3.8, Lemma 4.9 and Corollary 4.10.\n\n\\bibitem{loginov2007}\nAlexey Loginov, Thomas Reps, and Mooly Sagiv.\n\\newblock Refinement-based verification for possibly-cyclic lists.\n\\newblock In {\\em Program Analysis and Compilation, Theory and Practice},\n  volume 4444 of {\\em Lecture Notes in Computer Science}. Springer, 2007.\n\\newblock Primary author version; Figure 8 and Section 5.\n\n\\bibitem{manna1987}\nZohar Manna and Richard Waldinger.\n\\newblock The deductive synthesis of imperative {LISP} programs.\n\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of the Sixth National Conference on Artificial\n  Intelligence (AAAI-87)}, 1987.\n\\newblock Primary proceedings version; reversal programs on printed page 159.\n\n\\bibitem{pham2015}\nTrung~Van Pham.\n\\newblock Orbits of rotor-router operation and stationary distribution of\n  random walks on directed graphs.\n\\newblock arXiv:1403.5875v8, 2015.\n\\newblock Version of 30 June 2015; Theorem 1.\n\n\\end{thebibliography}\n"
